    "image": "Edit the first image into a photorealistic documentary keyframe, 16:9 landscape. Image 1 is the authoritative Blender camera and rebuilt community centre architecture: preserve camera, perspective, exact purple chair rows and central aisle, floor, black stage, blank screen, truss, award table, MF TV posters and lava lamps. Remove ONLY the seated white/gray test mannequin and the thin floating green horizontal test strip on the right of the stage. Add exactly two real-looking fictional hosts in the central aisle, facing the camera and already walking gently toward it, side by side: Halinka on screen LEFT, Czeslaw on screen RIGHT, their feet about 2.8 metres from the camera. Their bodies must fit the clear aisle without intersecting seats. Image 2 Halinka portrait defines exact identity; Image 3 Halinka full body defines her 162cm height, burgundy textured cardigan, black blouse and trousers, gold earrings and layered necklaces. Image 4 Czeslaw portrait defines exact identity and glasses; Image 5 his full body defines 171cm height, rumpled dark suit, beige shirt, loose brown tie, dark shoes. These are the same people; preserve age, face and body proportions. Halinka has a small warm proud smile, left hand making a restrained welcoming gesture at waist height; Czeslaw has a reserved serious expression, arms naturally down, no props. Match their lighting to the neutral warm house lights and retain the architectural plate's exposure and color. Eye-level 24mm documentary lens, natural skin, slight fabric detail, no fashion retouching, clear deep background. No captions, reference-sheet labels, extra people, additional furniture, altered screen content, helmets, wounds or rubble. This is frame A of a continuous backward camera tracking shot; keep the hosts comfortably centered with architecture clearly visible around them.\n",
    "endFrameDescription": "Następna pozycja tej samej kamery i gospodarzy; fizyczna kontynuacja marszu o 1.45 m ku foyer.",
    "animation": "@Element1 is Halinka already on screen left; @Element2 is Czeslaw already on screen right. 0.0–3.0s: both hosts are already walking toward the camera at an unhurried normal pace, taking two short natural steps along the clear central aisle. Halinka gently lowers her raised right hand and turns her eyes toward Czeslaw; he keeps looking toward the camera. Camera: smoothly tracks backward about 1.45 metres at their walking speed, reaching the supplied End Frame exactly. Secondary: subtle cardigan and loose tie sway with their steps. Continuity: preserve both identities, clothes, left/right positions, chair rows, stage, logos and steady lighting. Avoid sliding feet, furniture morphing, new people, cuts, fades or zoom."
